 just  kind of wondering um you know we just  you talked earlier in this conversation  about the the rankings of where people  had you slotted and whatnot  when you were watching that and based on  the you know the fact that you your  accolades that you were able to collect  at alabama did that  did that annoy you upset you in any way  were you you know angry and eager to  kind of prove those rankings wrong  i mean it definitely put a chip on my  shoulder you know what i mean it  bothered me a little bit but  at the same time i'm not like i'm not a  media guy i'm not the type of dude to  get like  caught up in all that garbage because i  know what my films had about me  and the gm and the scouts they know that  as well you know what i mean so um  i'm just grateful that um you know they  watched that film and  um you know they saw me as  good enough to be this 17th overall pick  you know what i mean so  i'm more than excited to get to the  program and um and prove them right  not necessarily like prove the haters  the people who made all the mock drives  and all this stuff wrong but to prove  myself  and to raid this organization right  because i'm thankful and grateful for  them  alex when you go to a place like alabama  you're going to have to compete there's  star players all over the place  including offensive line  how important was it for you to get on  the field early but then also looking  back  playing some guard and tackle in terms  of your development and what you were  able to show the nfl playing both of  those positions  definitely it was important for me to  play early uh i didn't get to start as a  freshman but  um i accepted my role on the team  when like i didn't start as a freshman i  was a backup and i just got in my bag  and tried to uh  perfect my craft as much as i could you  know what i mean  and um just uh coming from a place like  that  and being around a lot of competition um  i feel like  that only drove me to be like even  greater because uh i'm  super competitive at nature you know  what i mean so i feel like it was a  it was a great fit it was a great a  great spot to be in you know what i mean  just like by nature  and the nature of the program so i feel  like it's a great fit and  as far as me playing uh tackle and guard  uh you know when uh  my sophomore year i was one of the best  five so i had to find a spot on that  line  and i feel like uh playing guard and  playing tackle you know what i mean that  just showed my  versatility and competitiveness as an  athlete and that's an old lineman you  know what i mean  um being on the field by any means uh  sacrificing  or my team and just um just being a dog  and competing in  being on the field to contribute to wins  so  alex jerry macdonald from the bay area  news group um  could you tell us about where you are  who you were with uh who who made the  call to you was it coach gruden and  coach miak  and you're wearing the raiders had do  you did you have 32 hats  were you ready for anybody to pick you  yes sir i did have  32 hats i was ready for anybody to pick  me and uh coach gruen he definitely did  call me  and i'm in pensacola florida i'm on the  beach it's my hometown and i was  surrounded by my uh friends and family  and uh  i couldn't thank them more for being him  for being here and supporting me  and it was a great overall experience  and a great drive  alex one last question from my  conversation with butch jones is he said  that the most underrated characteristic  you have is leadership  did mike and mayok and john gruden talk  to you about coming in and even though  you'll be a rookie just the leadership  you can offer  oh we did touch on it a little bit but  um not much  but uh i just want to say thank you to  coach jones  because as far as being a leader that  was definitely one thing that i wanted  to change about myself going from my  junior to my senior year  just trying to affect those around me  you know what i mean in a positive way  and always harping on the things that we  needed to do to be champions  and uh i feel like that went well by the  results of my senior season  when we came out to national  championships and looks like we have one  more question willie go ahead  hey willy ramirez with the associated  press in las vegas we go back  two questions you had said that uh you  had all the hats waiting you were  waiting on  on the call that moment you received the  call as you're be as you're watching the  draft but your name's not called there  but you get that call can you just maybe  take us a couple of things that were  said that that overall  that overwhelming feeling maybe the  words that were said to you and  just that exchange once you knew it was  official  i mean um to be honest uh it wasn't  really  overwhelming not that i wasn't excited  and extremely grateful  for the opportunity but um  you know i i controlled what i could  control you know what i mean so i was  ready for like any outcome  i feel like i did the best i could do  and when they called me  and when they called me i was calm i was  uh  ready to go as soon as i got a call i  was like i don't know who this is you  know what i mean but hey it's go  time you know what i mean so i was just  super grateful  elated at the opportunity and uh yeah  that's pretty much it  great thank you for your time alex  appreciate it congratulations sir i  appreciate it  you

